PLACEHOLDER KEY — DO NOT SHIP THIS.

This is a real, well-formed ed25519 public key in PKIX/PEM form, generated once
so the example compiles and so its verification path fails CLOSED rather than
appearing to work. The matching private key was never saved and does not exist,
so nothing can produce a signature this key will accept.

Replace it with your own before publishing a release:

    openssl genpkey -algorithm ed25519 -out update-private-key.pem
    openssl pkey -in update-private-key.pem -pubout -out update-public-key.pem

Then back up update-private-key.pem offline and never commit it. Losing it, or
shipping a public key that does not match it, permanently strands every
installed copy of your app with no remote fix. See ../../docs/auto-update.md.

